# Task List
// A to-do list:  type a task and add it, tick it off when it's done, delete it, and drag the tasks into order.
// Its tasks and their checklist are in Task.spell;  this file holds the app.
// They're kept on this device, so they're still there next time:  TaskList.api.spell says where.

## The app
// A header saying how many are left, the new task's field, then the list.

task list is an app
	"checklist" is a new checklist
	its "draft" is text
		// The next task's title, as the new task's field holds it
	its "active count" is the length of (tasks in the checklist where it is active)

	when creating it
		// The tasks kept on this device, in their order
		fill the checklist

	to fill the checklist
		// The first time, with none kept yet, a few to start with
		clear the checklist
		for task in (every task) sorted by its order
			add it to the checklist
		if the checklist is not empty return
		add the task "Add a task above"
		add the task "Tick it off when it's done"
		add the task "Drag a task by its handle to move it"
		add the task "Delete one with its button"
		set the done of the first task in the checklist to yes

	to add the task (title as text)
		// A new task at the end of the list, kept on this device
		set task to a new task with title = title
		add task to the tasks
		add task to the checklist
		set the order of task to the length of the checklist

	to add the draft
		// The draft, as a new task;  the field empties
		if the draft is "" return
		add the task the draft
		clear the draft

	to draw it
		<container>
			<stack>
				<stack direction="horizontal" justify="between">
					<header level="2">Task List</header>
					<text color="grey">
						<if the active count is 0>All done<otherwise>{the active count} to do</>
					</text>
				</stack>
				<form value={it}>
					<input name="draft" placeholder="Something to do" aria-label="New task" fluid action>
						<button slot="action" color="primary" disabled={the draft is ""} onClick={add the draft}>Add</button>
					</input>
				</form>
				{draw the checklist}
			</stack>
		</container>
